    "what": "Troncal corridor each station physically sits on.",
    "source": "markers[].line.name from tramites.transmilenio.gov.co/station-maps/api/map (the same official source as plano_vagones.json). Only the corridor name is stored.",
    "why": "The direction a platform serves is named after the corridor, not after the compass — see corridor_directions.json.",
    "generated": "2026-08-12",
    "stations": 156,
    "letters_what": "Troncal letter of each corridor name above — the letter its route codes carry and the key the app colours a corridor by (spec 5.4.3).",
    "letters_source": "letra_trazado_troncal joined on troncal from ArcGIS Troncal/consulta_trazados_troncales (20 trazados, 12 distinct corridors). Every name here matched one, accent- and case-folded, with the single alias Autonorte = AUTOPISTA NORTE. TransMICable is not a troncal and gets none.",
    "letters_generated": "2026-08-15",
    "manual_what": "Stations the station-maps API has not published yet, filed by hand from the operator's own corridor name. Remove an entry once the API carries it.",
    "manual": {
      "TM90009": "Av. Ciudad de Cali",
      "TM90010": "Av. Ciudad de Cali",
      "TM90011": "Av. Ciudad de Cali"
    },
    "soacha": "The five stations past Portal Sur — TM0149 Bosa, TM0100 La Despensa, TM0101 Leon XIII, TM0102 Terreros, TM0103 San Mateo — are filed under the corridor SOACHA with letter S, not under NQS Sur where the station-maps API still puts them. The operator has re-lettered the services that run out there: S41, S42, S43, S45, S46 and S48 all appear in the 2026-08-28 catalog, and Toberin's own plano now carries S Troncal Soacha in its legend. The letter S is deliberately given G's cyan rather than a colour of its own. These services ride the NQS Sur trunk out of the city; a separate colour would draw one busway as two, which is the same reasoning that keeps Z on F's red. What changes is the NAME on the estacion page, because that is what the signage and the rider call it."
  },
